   "notes": "25 Petty Cury, north side, two frontages: west ~6.4 m Timpson, red brick, three bays of sash windows with stone lintels on 3 upper floors; east ~4 m narrow white-rendered house (Pylones in 2015, Phone World in 2020) with paired round-arched windows on the first and second floors under a moulded cornice. Single wall colour (brick) used for both. Assignment of OSM split to shops inferred from widths (25-27 = 7.6 m Body Shop, 25 = 10.6 m Timpson + Phone World, 24 = 6.0 m Halifax). Vertical dimensions squeezed to fit the 9.3 m DSM eave (photo suggests ~11 m)."
